On Wed, 1 Feb 2006, L wrote:

> I mention in the patch header that, though it works fine, it produces
> some compiler warnings that I can't quite work out. Do any of you C
> artists know what might be the cause?

If you don't include prototypes, functions are assumed to return ints. To
remove this warning, for example, for weaphitmsg, either add it to
include/extern.h, or declare it locally in mhitm.c:

extern const char *weaphitmsg(struct obj *obj,boolean uhitm);

